"; BLACK -- native in-game menus.\r\n;\r\n; This file is read when a menu opens: edit it while the game runs, then open the menu again.\r\n; Delete it to get the original layout back (the game writes it again). A page that is not listed\r\n; here, or has an error (see the log), is shown by the game itself. RECOMP_NATIVE_MENUS=0 turns\r\n; the native pages off.\r\n;\r\n; Pages have the game's own names. Positions are in the original 640 x 480 menu space (the menu\r\n; is centred on the picture at any aspect ratio); a text's Y is the top of its capitals.\r\n;\r\n; Text:     $KEY     the game's own words (language file), e.g. $FE_CONTINUE\r\n;           &KEY     text the game fills in (objective, warning), e.g. &FE_CURRENTOBJECTIVE\r\n;           \"...\"    your own words\r\n;           @name    a menu variable (see set)\r\n; Items:    item   = TEXT | ACTIONS [| if VALUE] [| unless VALUE] [| focus ACTIONS] [| gap N]\r\n;           toggle = TEXT | VALUE | FUNCTION              ON / OFF, sends FUNCTION(1 or 0)\r\n;           slider = TEXT | VALUE | FUNCTION | MIN MAX STEP\r\n;           keybind / padbind = TEXT | ACTION, padlayout = TEXT   the Controls pages (see [page Controls])\r\n;           photo = TEXT | fov/roll/weapon/speed/range   a photo mode setting (see [page PhotoMode])\r\n;           VALUE is a number the game publishes to its menus (FEInvertLookFlag ...).\r\n; Actions:  gamecode NAME [ARG ...]   one of the game's menu functions, as the original page calls it\r\n;           page NAME                  go to another page\r\n;           set NAME VALUE             remember a value for another page (read it as @NAME)\r\n;           video                      open the Video Settings page\r\n;           back                       this page's back action\r\n;           open NAME                  show a page of this file that the game does not have, over this one\r\n;           close                      leave such a page (back to the one it was opened over)\r\n;           exit                       close the game, as closing its window does\r\n;           Several actions are separated by ';' (keep comments on their own lines).\r\n; Page settings: title, label/text X Y TEXT [| wrap W], list X Y STEP, columns X1 X2, focus N,\r\n; back ACTIONS, start back|confirm (the pad's START), prompts select confirm back, arrows 2|4,\r\n; logo X Y, title_at X Y, prompts_at X Y STEP, rails X1 X2, selector WIDTH, loading VALUE,\r\n; require NAME (only when an earlier page set it).\r\n\r\n[style]\r\n; Colours are RRGGBB or AARRGGBB; they match the original pages as this port shows them.\r\nshade = D9091010\r\ncolumn = 1E1F201E\r\nrail = 5A6057\r\nitem = 36473D\r\nfocus = 7E7E7E\r\nlabel = 36473D\r\ntext = 7F7F7F\r\ntitle = 7F7F7F\r\nprompt = 7F7F7F\r\nselector = F0090B0A\r\nline = 7F7F7F\r\nchoice = 36473D\r\nchoice_on = 7F7F7F\r\nbullet = 36473D\r\nbullet_on = 7F7F7F\r\nfocus_scale = 1.1\r\nsounds = on\r\n\r\n[page PauseMenu]\r\ntitle = $FE_PAUSEMENU\r\nlabel = 284 141 $FE_CURRENTOBJECTIVES\r\ntext = 284 165 &FE_CURRENTOBJECTIVE | wrap 300\r\nlist = 285 241 25\r\nfocus = 1\r\nstart = back\r\nback = gamecode ClosePauseMenu\r\nloading = FELoadingPauseMenus\r\nitem = $FE_CONTINUE | gamecode ClosePauseMenu\r\nitem = $FE_OBJECTIVESSTATUS | page PauseMenuObjectives\r\nitem = $FE_RESTARTMISSION | set FEConfirmYesGameCode RestartLevel; set FEConfirmNoPage PauseMenu; page ConfirmWarning; gamecode SetupConfirmWarning RestartConfirm\r\nitem = $FE_OPTIONS | page PauseMenuOptionXbox\r\nitem = \"PHOTO MODE\" | open PhotoMode\r\nitem = $FE_QUIT | set FEConfirmYesGameCode QuitLevel; set FEConfirmNoPage PauseMenu; page ConfirmWarning; gamecode SetupConfirmWarning QuitConfirm\r\n\r\n[page PauseMenuOptionXbox]\r\ntitle = $FE_OPTIONS\r\nlogo = 185.5 58\r\ntitle_at = 199 86\r\nrails = 47 170\r\nlist = 218 147 27\r\ncolumns = 431 519\r\nselector = 349\r\narrows = 4\r\n; three rows more than the original page (CONTROLS, GAMEPLAY SETTINGS, VIDEO SETTINGS): the prompt